WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:05.301
Who's doing what, and are we on track? Make the plan together.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:10.815
The Plan tab opens on the plan board: Backlog, To do, Doing and Done, each with its

00:00:10.815 --> 00:00:12.449
stories and its points.

00:00:12.649 --> 00:00:16.136
The sprint chip says twenty-four points left, seven behind.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:22.720
New story asks what needs doing, where it goes, how big it is, who's on it, and a

00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:23.253
tag.

00:00:23.453 --> 00:00:25.331
Add it, and it lands in To do.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:33.451
Open a story to change it, move it on or mark it done.

00:00:33.651 --> 00:00:36.772
Mark the cabin done, and it moves to Done with a tick.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:46.248
When someone else adds a story, your open board shows it, without a reload.

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:55.940
The burn-down shows the points left each day against the ideal line.

00:00:56.140 --> 00:01:00.721
At this week's pace, the plan finishes on September thirtieth, four days late.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:06.868
Beside the chart, the biggest stories still open.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:16.765
The Popkin home shows the plan at a glance, and the recap counts the stories done.

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:25.256
On a phone, one column at a time, swiped sideways, with New story floating.

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:29.161
On a desktop, all four columns side by side.

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:39.017
Plan has a switch. While it is off, the tab is gone and its screens say so. Nothing

00:01:39.017 --> 00:01:39.801
is lost.

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:47.035
What no screen shows: only whoever added a story, its owner or the Host may delete

00:01:47.035 --> 00:01:50.282
it, and a wrapped-up Popkin's plan is read only.

00:01:50.482 --> 00:01:53.432
Every open board follows each change, live.

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:58.569
That is journey twenty-one. Popkin is a platform for pop-up communities.
